# Data & license rules (non-negotiable)

This project's entire value rests on being legally clean. Break these and the project is worthless.

## What may enter the corpus

| Allowed | Condition |
|---|---|
| Public-domain text | Author died in or before **1965** (Indian law: life + 60 years). Record death year. |
| Creative Commons | CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA only. Record exact license + source URL. |
| ODbL data | Alar dictionary. Credit V. Krishna; derived dictionary data stays ODbL. |
| Government CC releases | Only items explicitly released under CC (e.g. Dept. of Kannada & Culture). |

**Never**: works by authors who died after 1965 (Kuvempu, Bendre, DVG, Karanth, Masti are all still copyrighted), text retyped from a modern printed edition (editorial copyright), scraped content from any website without an explicit license, news articles.

## Provenance is mandatory

Every book and every data source has a `provenance` block. `scripts/validate-corpus.ts` fails the build without it.

```json
"provenance": {
  "source": "https://kn.wikisource.org/wiki/...",
  "license": "public-domain",
  "licenseNote": "Author died 1601; text from Wikisource proofread edition",
  "author": "ಸರ್ವಜ್ಞ",
  "authorDied": 1601,
  "retrieved": "2026-09-02"
}
```

`license` is one of: `public-domain`, `CC0-1.0`, `CC-BY-4.0`, `CC-BY-SA-4.0`, `ODbL-1.0`.

## Clean-room code policy

- Do not copy code, schemas, or curated data from any other Kannada project (Vachana Sanchaya, Kanaja, Padakanaja, Alar's site code, etc.). Features and ideas are fine; implementations are written fresh here.
- Third-party **libraries** are fine if MIT/Apache/BSD/ISC licensed and listed in `package.json`.
- Our code: AGPL-3.0-or-later. Our original content/docs: CC BY-SA 4.0.
